WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.696 --> 00:00:15.864
The dogs kept barking at me and I was afraid to move.

2
00:00:16.965 --> 00:00:20.908
Then a man called out of the window of the house, "Calm down, boys!

3
00:00:21.188 --> 00:00:21.728
Who's there?"

4
00:00:21.748 --> 00:00:23.910
"It's me," I said.

5
00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.351
"Who's me?"

6
00:00:25.971 --> 00:00:26.552
asked the voice.

7
00:00:26.572 --> 00:00:28.914
"George Jackson, sir.

8
00:00:29.674 --> 00:00:30.415
I'm only a boy."

9
00:00:30.435 --> 00:00:32.096
"What do you want?"

10
00:00:33.288 --> 00:00:34.369
"I don't want anything, sir.

11
00:00:35.409 --> 00:00:38.930
I only want to pass by the house, but the dogs won't let me."

12
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:43.592
"Why are you prowling around here at this time of night, huh?"

13
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:44.653
he asked.

14
00:00:44.673 --> 00:00:47.094
"I wasn't prowling around, sir."

15
00:00:48.154 --> 00:00:50.695
I began to make up a story in my head to tell him.

16
00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:53.697
"I fell overboard off a steamboat."

17
00:00:53.717 --> 00:01:01.180
"Look here, if you're telling the truth, you needn't be afraid," said the man in a kinder voice.

18
00:01:02.364 --> 00:01:03.465
"Nobody will hurt you."

19
00:01:04.665 --> 00:01:08.346
Then he shouted, "Bob and Tom, wake up and fetch the guns!"

20
00:01:09.327 --> 00:01:11.708
I heard more people moving around in the house.

21
00:01:12.648 --> 00:01:14.349
Then the man called out to me again.

22
00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:17.710
"George Jackson, do you know the Shepherdsons?"

23
00:01:19.571 --> 00:01:21.632
"No sir," I said truthfully.

24
00:01:21.652 --> 00:01:23.172
"I never heard of them."

25
00:01:23.192 --> 00:01:28.795
"Well, then, walk forward slowly and push the door open, just enough to squeeze in."

26
00:01:29.935 --> 00:01:31.996
I took one slow step at a time.

27
00:01:33.116 --> 00:01:37.459
As I got close to the front door, I heard the people inside unlocking it.

28
00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.241
I pushed it and stepped inside.

29
00:01:41.402 --> 00:01:46.185
By candlelight I could see three big men, all with guns pointed at me.

30
00:01:47.286 --> 00:01:50.668
The oldest was about sixty; the other two were young men.

31
00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:54.731
Behind them were an old lady and two younger women.

32
00:01:55.852 --> 00:01:59.414
As soon as I was inside, the old gentleman locked the door again.

33
00:02:00.355 --> 00:02:02.136
Then all of us went into the parlor.

34
00:02:03.564 --> 00:02:07.708
They all took a good look at me and decided that I didn't look like a Shepherdson.

35
00:02:08.709 --> 00:02:10.810
The old lady noticed that I was all wet.

36
00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:15.494
She told her servant girl to get me some food and to wake up Buck.

37
00:02:16.415 --> 00:02:19.158
Buck came down a few minutes later, rubbing his eyes.

38
00:02:20.259 --> 00:02:22.701
He looked to be about 13—my age.

39
00:02:24.202 --> 00:02:27.285
Buck took me up to his room where he gave me some dry clothes.

40
00:02:28.426 --> 00:02:30.888
He told me about a rabbit he had caught in the woods.

41
00:02:31.996 --> 00:02:36.540
Then he asked me where Moses was when the candle went out.

42
00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.342
I said I didn't know, and he said I should guess.

43
00:02:39.362 --> 00:02:43.986
"How can I guess," I said, "when I never heard of it before?"

44
00:02:45.328 --> 00:02:47.930
Finally he said, "He was in the dark!"

45
00:02:49.031 --> 00:02:51.593
"Well, if you knew where he was, why did you ask me?"

46
00:02:52.394 --> 00:02:52.794
I said.

47
00:02:52.814 --> 00:02:55.236
"It's a riddle," he said.

48
00:02:55.696 --> 00:02:56.697
Then he grinned at me.

49
00:02:56.717 --> 00:02:58.799
"Are you going to stay here awhile?

50
00:02:59.159 --> 00:02:59.760
I hope so.

51
00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.141
I have a dog and we can go down to the river and have great times."

52
00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:09.022
Still talking in this friendly way, he took me down to dinner.

53
00:03:10.163 --> 00:03:16.224
It was the best food I had ever tasted: cornbread and butter and beef and buttermilk.

54
00:03:17.565 --> 00:03:23.046
All the family members—their name was Grangerford, I soon found out—asked me questions.

55
00:03:25.207 --> 00:03:31.304
I told them I came from Arkansas, that my mother and brother and sisters were all dead, and

56
00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:36.308
that my father had drowned when we both fell off the steamboat, so I had no family.

57
00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:40.652
They said that I could have a home with them as long as I wanted.

58
00:03:42.253 --> 00:03:45.716
The Grangerfords lived in a beautiful house with lots of rooms.

59
00:03:46.937 --> 00:03:50.680
Everything was kept clean and polished by all their black servants.

60
00:03:51.721 --> 00:03:55.744
They had a clock on the mantel, with a china cat and dog on either side.

61
00:03:56.885 --> 00:03:59.968
They had many books and lots of pictures on the walls.

62
00:04:01.328 --> 00:04:05.972
Colonel Grangerford, the older man, treated his family kindly, and they loved him.

63
00:04:06.892 --> 00:04:10.955
He and his two grown-up sons were handsome men and very well dressed.

64
00:04:11.896 --> 00:04:14.077
His wife was a sweet-faced kind lady.

65
00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:21.203
The two daughters were Miss Charlotte, who was proud, and Miss Sophia, who was quiet and gentle.

66
00:04:22.384 --> 00:04:27.587
I found out that the family used to be larger, but a daughter had died, and three sons

67
00:04:27.627 --> 00:04:28.228
had been killed.

68
00:04:29.772 --> 00:04:33.573
One day Buck and I were walking in the woods when we heard a horse coming.

69
00:04:33.593 --> 00:04:35.374
"Quick, hide!"

70
00:04:36.014 --> 00:04:36.514
Buck said.

71
00:04:37.414 --> 00:04:41.455
We hid behind a tree and saw a handsome young horseman with a gun.

72
00:04:42.516 --> 00:04:46.337
I later found out his name was Harney, and he was one of the Shepherdsons.

73
00:04:47.677 --> 00:04:52.698
Suddenly Buck fired his gun, right by my ear, and Harney's hat flew off his head.

74
00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:58.120
Then we both ran through the woods and didn't stop until we got back to the house.

75
00:04:59.228 --> 00:05:02.590
Colonel Grangerford scolded Buck for shooting from behind a tree.

76
00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.632
"But that's what the Shepherdsons do," Buck replied.

77
00:05:07.913 --> 00:05:12.916
I noticed that Miss Sophia looked very pale until she heard that Harney Shepherdson wasn't hurt.

78
00:05:13.816 --> 00:05:18.519
When Buck and I were by ourselves, I asked him why he wanted to hurt Harney Shepherdson.

79
00:05:18.539 --> 00:05:20.259
"What did he do to you?"

80
00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:21.280
I asked.

81
00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.862
"He never did anything to me," Buck answered.

82
00:05:24.882 --> 00:05:27.683
"Well, why did you want to shoot at him?"

83
00:05:28.204 --> 00:05:28.604
I asked.

84
00:05:29.568 --> 00:05:34.209
Then Buck told me that there was a feud between the Grangerfords and the Shepherdsons.

85
00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:41.792
I had never heard this word before, so he explained that long ago, a man in one family

86
00:05:42.112 --> 00:05:45.173
had fought with a man in the other family, and killed him.

87
00:05:46.653 --> 00:05:49.154
Then the dead man's brother shot the first man.

88
00:05:50.194 --> 00:05:53.055
Then all the brothers and cousins got into the fight, too.

89
00:05:54.055 --> 00:05:56.536
The feud had started more than thirty years ago.

90
00:05:57.841 --> 00:06:01.552
No one could remember who had started the first fight, or what it was about.

91
00:06:02.635 --> 00:06:03.678
But the feud went on.
